PATCH 333: thread the c68c=mga:0x2004 (cockpit-instrument bbox analyzer) method-vector args in the two
callers FUN_1000_7a98 (windshield, container 0x8e84, children 0x8e91/0x8ead/0x8ec9) and FUN_0000_767c
(reticle sources, container 0x8d54, children 0x8d60/0x8d2c/0x8d10).  asm 0x17ab1/0x767c: al=id, bx=child,
si=container (DGROUP near offsets -> host ptrs).  Ghidra's __allregs indirect dispatch dropped every
register arg, so the calls were arg-less no-ops (patch 301/302 left them so because DGROUP:0x68c was 0);
patch 331 restores 0x68c=mga:0x2004, so without the args these would dispatch the analyzer on garbage
registers.  767c also gets its d594/c560/c6a8 args threaded (identical idiom to 7a98/patch 301, it was
pristine).  Together with 331 (un-zero 0x68c) + 332 (reconstruct 2004) this populates the reticle geometry
DGROUP:0x156c to 288x81.  Mission-path only -> behaviour-neutral for the 24 menu/settings flows.

